"""Tool descriptions (MCP and /api/tools)."""
DOCS = {'lookup_rates': 'Negotiated rates for one billing code in one US state, one row per payer product, provider group (TIN) and price.\n\nArgs:\n    code: billing code, e.g. CPT/HCPCS "99213", "70553", MS-DRG "470"; a comma list works too\n    state: two-letter state where the provider practices, e.g. "TX" (Aetna: 3 networks nationwide)\n    payer: "cigna", "aetna", "uhc", a comma list, or "all"\n    network: optional filter on product/network/plan/employer name, e.g. "Choice Plus", "OAP", "UNITED AIRLINES"\n    city: optional practice city (NPPES), e.g. "Austin"\n    zip_prefix: optional ZIP prefix, e.g. "787" or "78701"\n    specialty: optional NUCC taxonomy text or code, e.g. "Orthopaedic Surgery", "Family Medicine", "207X00000X"\n    provider: optional TIN (9 digits), NPI (10 digits) or provider name\n    billing_class: optional "professional" or "institutional"\n    limit: max rows (default 200)\nReturns rows with payer, product, tin, provider, npis_in_area, rate, negotiated_type, billing_class, setting,\nmodifiers, place_of_service, medicare, pct_of_medicare.\nWhen `provider` is given, the provider\'s flat "all services" arrangements (code type CSTM-ALL, e.g. UHC\'s\nper-visit "PRO" rate for some urgent care groups) are included too. Radiology and other split services carry\nmodifier 26 (professional) / TC (technical) rows next to the global rate.', 'market_distribution': 'Distribution of negotiated rates for a code in a state: provider-group count, min/p10/p25/median/p75/p90/max,\nmean, Medicare amount and median % of Medicare. Each provider group counts once (its median published amount).\n\nArgs:\n    code: billing code, e.g. "99213"\n    state: two-letter state, e.g. "NY"\n    payer: "cigna", "aetna", "uhc", comma list, or "all"\n    network: optional product/network/plan filter\n    city: optional practice city\n    zip_prefix: optional ZIP prefix\n    specialty: optional taxonomy text or code (peer group)\n    billing_class: "professional" (default), "institutional" or "" for both\n    group_by: "payer" (default), "product", "setting" or "none"\n    place: "office" (default: base rates with no modifiers that apply in an office or anywhere),\n        "facility" (facility places of service) or "any" (every published amount, incl. modifiers 52/55/56/26/TC)\n    modifier: "" (unmodified/global rate, default), "26" (professional reading) or "TC" (technical component);\n        use this rather than run_sql for component-level distributions', 'provider_rates': 'FASTEST way to get one provider\'s rates for many codes (one call; use it instead of looping lookup_rates).\nRows collapse networks that pay the same amount; each row has payer, tin, code, modifiers (26 = professional\nreading, TC = technical, blank = global), negotiated_type, rate, medicare, pct_of_medicare, networks count.\nAlso returns the provider\'s flat all-services arrangements (code_type CSTM-ALL) if the payer uses one.\n\nArgs:\n    provider: NPI (10 digits), TIN (9 digits) or name; resolve names with search_providers first if unsure\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes (up to 50), e.g. "70450,70460,70551,71046"\n    state: two-letter state where the provider practices\n    payer: "cigna", "aetna", "uhc", comma list, or "all" (Aetna: 3 networks nationwide)\n    network: optional product/network filter', 'compare_providers': 'Side-by-side rates of several providers for several codes, per payer product (median of published amounts).\n\nArgs:\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes, e.g. "99213,99214,73721"\n    state: two-letter state\n    providers: comma-separated TINs, NPIs or provider names, e.g. "Baylor Scott,742664409"\n    payer: payer filter or "all"\n    network: optional product/network filter\n    place: "office" (default, base rates without modifiers), "facility" or "any"', 'benchmark_provider': 'How a provider\'s negotiated rates compare with peers in the same state (optionally same specialty):\nthe provider\'s rate, peer p25/median/p75, percentile rank and % of Medicare for each code and payer product.\nUse it for "how does my practice\'s contract compare" questions.\n\nArgs:\n    provider: TIN, NPI or name of the provider/practice\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes\n    state: two-letter state\n    payer: payer filter or "all"\n    specialty: optional peer specialty (taxonomy text or code)\n    network: optional product/network filter\n    place: "office" (default, base rates without modifiers), "facility" or "any"', 'network_breadth': 'How many clinicians (NPIs) and TINs in an area have published rates in each payer product/network,\nand their share of all NPPES clinicians there. Use for comparing network breadth.\n\nArgs:\n    state: two-letter state\n    specialty: optional taxonomy text or code, e.g. "Cardiovascular Disease"\n    city: optional practice city\n    zip_prefix: optional ZIP prefix\n    payer: payer filter or "all"\n    group_by: "product" (default) or "network"', 'provider_networks': 'Which payer products a provider has published rates in (by NPI, TIN, or name + state).\n\nArgs:\n    provider: NPI (10 digits), TIN (9 digits) or name\n    state: two-letter state (required when searching by name)', 'find_plans': 'Find networks by product, plan or employer name (Aetna publishes plan/employer names; Cigna and UHC name\nfiles by product), e.g. "Choice POS II", "MCKESSON", "Options PPO", "OAP".\n\nArgs:\n    query: text to search\n    payer: payer filter or "all"', 'list_products': 'The payer products (network families) loaded, with network and plan counts.\n\nArgs:\n    payer: payer filter or "all"', 'search_providers': 'Search clinicians/organizations in NPPES (by NPI, or name/specialty/city within a state) and show the TINs\npayers list them under. Use to resolve a provider name to NPI/TIN before other tools.\n\nArgs:\n    name: provider or organization name (substring)\n    state: two-letter state (required unless npi is given)\n    specialty: taxonomy text, e.g. "Dermatology"\n    city: practice city\n    npi: a 10-digit NPI\n    limit: max rows', 'code_info': 'Which payers publish a billing code, its type, published text where licensable (CPT text is withheld),\nand national Medicare physician fee schedule amounts.\n\nArgs:\n    code: billing code', 'medicare_rate': 'Medicare physician fee schedule amounts (CY2026, non-facility and facility) for comma-separated HCPCS/CPT\ncodes: national ("US") or adjusted by the state\'s mean locality GPCI.\n\nArgs:\n    codes: comma-separated codes, e.g. "99213,99214"\n    state: two-letter state or "US" (national)', 'data_status': 'What data is loaded (payers, products, networks) and whether the app is ready.', 'rank_providers': 'Rank provider groups (TINs) by negotiated rates across a basket of codes, in one state or NATIONALLY\n(state "US", every state). Each group\'s rate per code is its median published office/base rate; the basket is\ncombined as a weighted average (dollars) and a weighted average % of national Medicare. Use it for questions like\n"highest-paid radiology groups in the nation" (codes = the specialty\'s common CPTs, weights = their relative\nvolume if known). National runs cover Cigna and UHC by default (Aetna\'s national files are heavy).\n\nArgs:\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes (up to 20), e.g. "70450,70553,71250,72148,74177,77067"\n    state: two-letter state, a comma list of states, or "US" for national (default). A national run that\n        runs out of time lists states_not_done in the first (summary) row: call again with those and merge\n    payer: "cigna,uhc" (default), "cigna", "uhc", "aetna" or "all"\n    specialty: optional filter on the group\'s main NPPES classification, e.g. "Radiology"\n    weights: optional comma-separated weights in the same order as codes (e.g. annual volumes); default equal\n    place: "office" (default), "facility" or "any"\n    modifier: "" (global/unmodified, default), "26" (professional reading) or "TC" (technical)\n    min_codes: minimum codes a group must have rates for (default: half of the codes)\n    limit: how many top groups to return (default 25)'}
